messages.content:
Write authorization-inquiry/v1 from this CURRENT natural brief. Do not answer the source question, infer code behavior, add an expectation, future policy or unprovided premises.
Fields: schemaVersion, mode behavior|conformance, questions:[{id,request,principal?,resource?,operation?,entryHint?,premises:[{text,origin:user}]}], optional policy:{text,origin:user|external-policy,location} only for conformance.
Keep every requested scenario in question.request or a separate question. Optional principal/resource/operation are task wording, never invented code facts. Unspecified facts remain unspecified. Conformance copies the independently supplied policy verbatim.
Unrelated synthetic example: {schemaVersion:'authorization-inquiry/v1',mode:'behavior',questions:[{id:'museum',request:'Can a visitor reserve an exhibit?',premises:[]}]}. This is a structural example with no source answer.

Current mode: conformance
Current user policy: {"text":"A caller creating a document share must have view_document permission for the exact shared document. A global add_sharelink permission or knowing a document ID alone is insufficient.","origin":"user","location":"experimental-user-brief:paperless-share-policy/v1"}
Current natural brief:
Check creating a share through ShareLinkViewSet against the current independently supplied policy. A principal asks to share an existing document; determine which endpoint and object controls apply to that exact document before the share is created. Include relevant inherited permission and serializer paths. Do not assume that document existence or a global model permission grants access to this document. Explain source behavior, policy compliance and specific missing facts.

You MUST respond with a valid JSON object conforming to this schema:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "schemaVersion": {
      "type": "string",
      "const": "authorization-inquiry/v1"
    },
    "mode": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "behavior",
        "conformance"
      ]
    },
    "questions": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "request": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "principal": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "resource": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "operation": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "entryHint": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          },
          "premises": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "text": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1
                },
                "origin": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "const": "user"
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "text",
                "origin"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id",
          "request",
          "premises"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "minItems": 1,
      "maxItems": 16
    },
    "policy": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "text": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1
        },
        "origin": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "user",
            "external-policy"
          ]
        },
        "location": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "text",
        "origin",
        "location"
      ],
      "additionalProperties": false
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "schemaVersion",
    "mode",
    "questions"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

Output ONLY the JSON object, nothing else. No markdown fences, no explanation.

